  "question": {
    "text": "A power transmission line feeds input power at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2300</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> to a step down transformer with its primary windings having <math><mn>4000</mn></math> turns. The output power is delivered at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>230</mn><mi>&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> by the transformer. If the current in the primary of the transformer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> and its efficiency is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>90</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>%</mi></math>, the output current would be:"
  },
